{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "feed_key": "uz_brand_allowlist",
  "description": "Uzbekistan bank / payment / government / telecom brands that are impersonated by malware and phishing in-region. Consumed by BOTH the APK impersonation check (android.packages + android.signing_cert_sha256) and the URL typosquat/homograph check (domains).",
  "provisioning_contract": {
    "domains": "Registrable domains are the high-confidence part of this file and are safe to ship as-is. They drive URL typosquatting and homograph detection.",
    "android.packages": "The brand's own Google Play app ids. package_verified=true means every id in the list was confirmed on its Google Play listing — published by the brand's official developer account, with the brand's title — on the date in package_provenance. package_verified=false means the list has NOT been confirmed; such ids may drive only brand-name similarity signals, never a cert mismatch, and an empty list means no official Play app was found. All of a brand's own apps that carry its name are listed (consumer, business and companion apps) so the package-lookalike check can never flag the brand's second app as an imitation of its first. Unrelated apps the same account publishes (games, media, e-learning, HR tools) are left out on purpose: nobody imitates them, and every extra short id widens the lookalike net for everyone else's apps. White-label ids whose only distinguishing part is a two- or three-letter bank code (uz.fb.cib.mobile.aab, com.bssys.mbcphone.uz.ofb) are left out for the same reason: another bank's app built on the same vendor platform with a similar short code would sit within lookalike distance of it.",
    "android.package_provenance": "Audit trail for android.packages, one row per id: the Play listing's title, publisher, publisher website and non-generic support-email domain as seen on the checked date. Informational only — the engines ignore it. Re-check it when a brand rebrands or moves an app to another developer account (uz.kapitalbank.android is Uzum Bank today, published by Uzum).",
    "known_clashes": "Real Android package ids that sit within lookalike distance of a listed android.packages id without imitating it — the same operator or marketplace in another country (kz/kg/ge/am.beeline.odp next to uz.beeline.odp), or an unrelated app one edit away (com.ozon, com.ison next to com.oson). The APK identity check reports no package-lookalike for an exact member. Add an id here only after confirming on its Play listing that it is published by that other company; an id listed in error is an id the lookalike check can never flag.",
    "android.signing_cert_sha256": "pin_status=unpinned means we hold no signing-certificate pin. The APK impersonation check CANNOT report IMPERSONATION_CERT_MISMATCH for an unpinned brand — see ApkImpersonationCheck. Pins are provisioned with tools/allowlist-provision.mjs from an APK obtained through an official channel. Pins are per brand, not per package: before a brand with several packages is marked pinned, the signing certificate of EVERY listed package must be provisioned (one APK per package, --add after the first), otherwise the brand's own other apps would be reported as counterfeits. Pinning the payment brands first (Payme, Click, Humo, Uzcard, Uzum) retires the origin heuristic DEV_BRAND_PACKAGE_SIDELOADED, which exists only because an exact brand-package match currently concludes nothing: with a pin, the same app is judged on its certificate instead.",
    "release_gate": "tools/check-allowlist.mjs fails a release build if any entry is referenced by cert-mismatch logic while still unpinned."
  },
  "trusted_suffixes": [
    {
      "suffix": "gov.uz",
      "note": "Public suffix, NOT a registrable domain — it must never be treated as an allowlist domain for typosquat distance (every *.gov.uz name would be distance 0 from it). Listed here so that a host under it can be reported as government-operated, and so that a lookalike of the suffix itself (g0v.uz, gov-uz.com) is flagged."
    }
  ],
  "known_clashes": [
    "kz.beeline.odp",
    "kg.beeline.odp",
    "ge.beeline.odp",
    "am.beeline.odp",
    "com.ozon",
    "com.ison"
  ],
